<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Lal Meri Pat, in Jabroo (Ashiq Hussain; sung by Inayat Hussain Bhatti, Fazal Hussain, A. R. Bismil)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1956</span><span class="sg-chain-h">new melody for a film</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Dama Dam Mast Qalandar, in Dillan Dey Soudey (Noor Jehan; modified by Nazir Ali)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1969</span><span class="sg-chain-h">film version on Hussain's melody, the most popular</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Nasbandi (Amit Kumar)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1978</span><span class="sg-chain-h">sung in the film</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Dam Mast Mast (Nusrat Fateh Ali Khan, M. Arshad)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1991</span><span class="sg-chain-h">new song inspired by it, different melody</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Boxer (Nusrat Fateh Ali Khan)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1992</span><span class="sg-chain-h">his song performed in the film, in Punjabi and Urdu</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Tu Cheez Badi Hai Mast Mast, in Mohra (Viju Shah; Kavita Krishnamurthy, Udit Narayan)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1994</span><span class="sg-chain-h">adapted from Nusrat Fateh Ali Khan's version</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Hum Hain Bemisaal (Baba Sehgal, Alka Yagnik)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1994</span><span class="sg-chain-h">sung in the film</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">D-Day (Mika Singh)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2013</span><span class="sg-chain-h">sung in the film</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">David (Rekha Bhardwaj)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2013</span><span class="sg-chain-h">sung in the film</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Barakah (Sami Yusuf)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2016</span><span class="sg-chain-h">cover of Nusrat Fateh Ali Khan's song</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Cheez Badi, in Machine (Neha Kakkar, Udit Narayan)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2017</span><span class="sg-chain-h">remake of the Mohra song</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Coke Studio Bangla (Runa Laila)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2025</span><span class="sg-chain-h">performance</span></li></ul></section>
